---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SocialIcon from '../components/SocialIcon.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../lib/site';
import { getPosts } from '../lib/posts';

const posts = await getPosts();
const tags = new Set(posts.flatMap((p) => p.data.tags));
---

<Base title="About" description="Data studies run with AI agents: why this blog exists and how to reach the author.">
  <section class="wrap about">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>If AI takes over the routine, <span class="grad">we get to create.</span></h1>

    <div class="intro card">
      <p>
        So I started this blog. Here I run data studies with the help of <strong>AI agents</strong>: they collect sources,
        clean the data and do the heavy lifting, and I ask the questions, check the numbers and decide what the results mean.
      </p>
      <p>
        Maybe the findings will be useful to you. Read along, and if you have questions or ideas for the next study,
        message me on social media.
      </p>
      <p class="sign">— {AUTHOR.name}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat card">
        <p class="value">{posts.length}</p>
        <p class="label">{posts.length === 1 ? 'study' : 'studies'} published</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat card">
        <p class="value">{tags.size}</p>
        <p class="label">topics tagged</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat card">
        <p class="value">100%</p>
        <p class="label">of the data linked</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How every study works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="n">1</span>
        <div><strong>A question.</strong> Something concrete, like which CPU brand gives more performance per dollar.</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">2</span>
        <div><strong>Data, collected by agents.</strong> Every number keeps a link to its source, and raw pages are saved.</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">3</span>
        <div><strong>Analysis in Python.</strong> Plain scripts, so each result can be re-run and checked.</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">4</span>
        <div><strong>A human check.</strong> I review the method, the outliers and the claims before anything is published.</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">5</span>
        <div>
          <strong>A live follow-up.</strong> When a study is about listed companies, the post shows their share price on the day
          it was published next to the live price, so you can see how the story plays out.
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <div class="socials">
      {
        AUTHOR.socials.map((s) => (
          <a class={`social card ${s.icon}`} href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener me">
            <span class="icon">
              <SocialIcon name={s.icon} size={20} />
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="net">{s.label}</span>
              <span class="handle">{s.handle}</span>
            </span>
            <span class="go" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.3em 0.75em;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: #fff;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-1), var(--accent-2));
  }
  h1 {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .grad {
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--accent-1), var(--accent-2));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
  }
  .intro {
    position: relative;
    padding: 28px 30px;
    margin: 28px 0 14px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .intro::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    width: 5px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--accent-1), var(--accent-2));
  }
  .intro p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .sign {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .stat {
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .stat .value {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .stat .label {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .intro {
      padding: 22px 20px 22px 24px;
    }
  }
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .steps li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .n {
    flex: none;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--accent-1);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-1) 12%, transparent);
  }
  .socials {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .socials {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .social {
    --c: #0a66c2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }
  .social.instagram {
    --c: #e1306c;
  }
  .social.github {
    --c: var(--ink);
  }
  .social.github .icon {
    color: var(--surface);
  }
  .social:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: #fff;
    background: var(--c);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px -6px var(--c);
  }
  .social.instagram .icon {
    background: linear-gradient(45deg, #f9a825, #e1306c 50%, #833ab4);
  }
  .net {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .handle {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .go {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
</style>
